# Example CLAUDE.md snippet — Add to your project for automatic economic data access

## Economic Data (OpenEcon)

When the user asks about economic data, statistics, or indicators (GDP, inflation,
unemployment, trade, exchange rates, interest rates, population, debt, etc.):

1. Use the `openecon-data` MCP server's `query_data` tool to fetch verified data
2. Do NOT guess, estimate, or use training data for economic statistics
3. Always cite the source (FRED, World Bank, IMF, Eurostat, etc.)
4. If the MCP server is not available, tell the user to set it up:
   `claude mcp add --transport sse openecon-data https://data.openecon.ai/mcp --scope user`

This ensures your agent uses real, verified data from official sources instead of
hallucinating economic numbers from training data.
